' 4+1 Scenarios (+1) - View Pokémon detail with evolutions and type matchups (US04)
' Version 1.1 - 2026-10-20 - reflects the current working tree
' Shows how the Logical view (PokemonDetailViewModel, PokemonRepository) and the Process view (parallel
' loads after the main data) support inspecting a Pokémon. Concurrency detail: process-open-pokemon-detail.puml.
' C4 equivalent: c4/dynamic-open-pokemon-detail.puml.
' Sprite and cry URLs come in the PokeAPI response; sprites are on PokeAPI/sprites and cries on PokeAPI/cries (GitHub raw).
@startuml scenarios-view-detail
!include ../style.puml

title Scenario - view Pokémon detail
autonumber

actor User
participant PokemonDetailScreen
participant PokemonDetailViewModel
participant PokemonRepository
participant PokeAPI <<external>>
database "Local Database" as LocalDb
participant "PokeAPI Sprites\n(GitHub raw)" as Sprites <<external>>
participant "PokeAPI Cries\n(GitHub raw)" as Cries <<external>>

User -> PokemonDetailScreen : taps a Pokémon in any list
PokemonDetailScreen -> PokemonDetailViewModel : observes pokemon
PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getPokemon(name)
PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET pokemon/{name}
PokemonRepository --> PokemonDetailViewModel : Pokemon
PokemonDetailViewModel --> PokemonDetailScreen : stats, sprites, abilities
par
    PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : isCaught(name)
    PokemonRepository -> LocalDb : SELECT EXISTS
else
    PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getEvolutionChain(species)
    PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET species, then chain
else
    PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getTypeEffectiveness(types)
    PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET type/{t} per type
end
PokemonDetailViewModel --> PokemonDetailScreen : star, evolutions, weaknesses
PokemonDetailScreen -> Sprites : loads sprites and evolution sprites (Coil)

User -> PokemonDetailScreen : toggles front/back, shiny, female
User -> PokemonDetailScreen : plays the cry
PokemonDetailScreen -> Cries : streams the cry .ogg (MediaPlayer)
User -> PokemonDetailScreen : taps an evolution
PokemonDetailScreen -> PokemonDetailScreen : opens that species (same scenario)
@enduml
